ith over the  moon i mean when you have  movies like crazy rich asians and and  tiger tail  and you know and the farewell and and  now  they're they're you know to me we're  breaking ground with um  with over the moon this is such a very  very big movie  and um just so unique in its scope and  breadth and  um you know with this very ancient story  but in a very modern take and you know  what a great cast  and what a beautiful beautiful  production it's just  it's very very big and i'm so proud to  be a part of it  i just knew that the content of the  script was going to be so moving to  people and i just  i saw the illustrations beforehand and  they were extraordinary  but the process of actually recording it  was so fun  glenn keane is just like the most loving  supportive man  um he's so fun to work with he really  plays with you  um he wants you to go all the way  you know be as free and as playful as  possible and then he reigns you in a bit  and gives you specificities and it's  just like such a fun  um a fun way to work as an actor i've  heard that glenn always has  a sketch pad with him that he's always  drawing  um how did you guys kind of see your  characters come to life over  however many recording sessions you had  and then finally seeing  the final product something that really  stuck out to me is that every  time that glenn drew her she looked  really powerful and grounded  even though she was only 12 years old  you know and so  from that i could already tell like they  face headstrong and  confident and driven and so his his  art really inspired me inspired the  character  you're working with the legend and um he  has a very unique style like in  animation where  when you're when you're doing when  you're in a voiceover booth you know  he was there with me like in in the room  and so you have that kind of intimacy of  directing him  and and it it allows you really to to  zero in on story you're not just kind of  like it's not like doing a voice-over ad  and doing it over and over again  you're you're doing something you know  everything you're saying any  anything comedic is going to is going to  serve us the story  he's just so um supportive and  so knowledgeable and just so aware of  exactly what you need  in there it's such a specific thing of  what an actor needs  inside of a booth when you're kind of  just like working  where you just don't know what it's  going to look like you don't know what  it's going to sound like and what it's  going to be like and none of the actors  are there  and it's just very strange but he knows  and  it's it's really amazing he's incredible  it was so exciting to meet him i mean  he's made some of my favorite  animations of all time um i think i  blacked out i i don't even remember what  i said  but um it was probably like hi  thanks for making this thanks for  including me i'm so honored i don't know  i really got to play and and bring all  of myself to it and  you know they were filming us during the  the recording process so  even in the film like there's like  certain looks i'm like  that's kind of a thing that i think i do  and i'm sure they took many  crazy things that i was doing in the  booth that day um  as inspiration for animating and i loved  that i thought that was so cool  he's just a master at storytelling uh  and i'm so  thankful for you know the characters  that he's  made an animation a large part of that  like inspired me  to to pursue art you know so  he's been he's been so influential to so  many people and i'm glad  that he could direct me because he  should be storytelling for the rest of  his life i i there's something about his  style that um  fosters just the sense of play it was  always  fun working with him in the studio and  he's also such a clear  um he has such clear visions of the  world around  you so for an actor he gave me  everything i needed and  i felt like i got to learn so much from  him when you saw it finished were you  completely  blown away it's just a beautiful  beautiful movie it's magnificent it's  really  it's just uh i think something that the  whole family can enjoy too  it's really special the chinese  landscape is beautiful and we're also  seeing  a lot of different chinese faces and  asian faces that all look a little  different but are all  true and then then you go to this  fantastic world  like it's insane and you see this moon  goddess dressed by guo pay and  the way she moves i mean it it  added so much for me to be able to see  what the world was it gave me a lot of  perspective  so helen park was one of the songwriters  and i had seen um a show k-pop that she  had worked on  and i was like okay so like i already  know what i gotta bring  to this because i know what helen  probably has in mind  so like you know there was there was  there was a lot of imagination  [Music]  like imaginary work that was happening  um  and of course the song itself is like  such a cool  song um but it really wasn't until like  i saw  the full animation that like my mind was  blown and i was like  i'm so cool i feel so  cool i've never felt so cool in my  life so so  i i was like oh this is so awesome and  and even better than that like  i know that none of that would have been  possible without the entire  collaboration collaboration and the  entire team it was just so beautiful  when they first showed me some of the  animation for rocket to the moon  i cried a lot um and then they had to  take a really long break  in the studio because like i was too  like snotty and everything  so i couldn't say my lines um it's a  perfect family film for this time i mean  i think that's something that is  inclusive  um diverse and has a cultural  specificity  for a global tale for something that's  universally accessible  at its core it's about life loss  and love and i think that you know you  the more specific you go culturally  the more fulfilling it is globally and  as well as artistically  so many actors talk